== Introduction
<introduction>
This lesson continues from Class 9's study of #strong[Tawaf al-Ziyarah
(طواف الزيارة)]. Having established the #strong[obligation],
#strong[rukn] (ḥuḍūr), and #strong[niyyah] requirement, the teacher now
examines the #strong[conditions (shurūṭ)] and #strong[wājibāt (واجبات)]
\[necessary acts\] of ṭawāf --- in particular #strong[ṭahārah (طهارة)]
\[ritual purity\], #strong[satr al-ʿawrah (ستر العورة)] \[covering the
private area\], #strong[najāsah (نجاسة)] \[external impurity\],
#strong[muwālāt (موالاة)] \[continuity\], #strong[muḥādhāt (محاذاة)]
\[proximity of a woman in prayer\], and the #strong[wājibāt] of walking,
starting from #strong[Ḥajar al-Aswad (الحجر الأسود)], and circling from
the #strong[right side]. The class also includes a foundational
discussion on the #strong[classification of ḥadīth reports] (khabar) and
their implications for fiqh rulings.

