#strong[Why is the compensation greater for janābah?]

- The #strong[defect] is #strong[greater] --- janābah is a more severe
  state of impurity than the absence of wuḍū.
- Greater defect → greater compensation.
- Without wuḍū = goat (شاة); without ghusl from janābah = badanah
  (بدنة).

=== Does the defective ṭawāf lift iḥrām restrictions?
<does-the-defective-awaf-lift-ihram-restrictions>
#strong[Yes.] According to the Ḥanafī school, because the ṭawāf is
#strong[valid] (though defective), it #strong[does lift the remaining
iḥrām restrictions] --- including the restriction on
#strong[physical/marital relations].

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (50%, 50%),
    align: (auto,auto,),
    table.header([Scenario], [Penalty?],),
    table.hline(),
