== Part 2 --- Najāsah (external impurity) on body or clothing
<part-2-najasah-external-impurity-on-body-or-clothing>
=== Ruling: Sunnah (to purify), not Farḍ or Wājib
<ruling-sunnah-to-purify-not-far-or-wajib>
- Purifying the body and clothing from #strong[external najāsah]
  (e.g.~impurity on clothes) is #strong[sunnah] for ṭawāf.
- If someone performs ṭawāf with najāsah on his body or clothing:
  #strong[no compensation (dam) is required].

=== Why no compensation?
<why-no-compensation>
- The prohibition of external najāsah relates to the #strong[masjid]
  (i.e.~the Masjid al-Ḥarām), #strong[not] to the #strong[ṭawāf] itself.
- Since the defect is not in the act of ṭawāf but in the context of
  being in the masjid, #strong[no defect appears in the ṭawāf] --- hence
  no dam.

