== Part 4 --- Muḥādhāt (woman standing parallel to a man)
<part-4-muhadhat-woman-standing-parallel-to-a-man>
=== In ṣalāh
<in-salah>
#strong[Muḥādhāt (محاذاة)] --- when a #strong[woman] stands
#strong[directly parallel/beside] a man, performing the #strong[same
ṣalāh] behind the #strong[same imam] --- it #strong[breaks the man's
ṣalāh] (not the woman's).

#strong[Key conditions for muḥādhāt to break ṣalāh:]

+ They must be performing the #strong[same ṣalāh] --- i.e.~behind the
  same imam, joined in the same congregation.
+ The imam must have made #strong[intention] to lead the woman.
+ She stands #strong[completely parallel] to the man (beside him, not
  behind).

#strong[When muḥādhāt does NOT break ṣalāh:]

- They are performing #strong[separate ṣalāhs] --- even if both are
  praying Ẓuhr, if they are not behind the same imam, there is no
  muḥādhāt issue.
- In #strong[Ṣalāt al-Janāzah] --- because it is not ṣalāh in the
  conventional sense (no rukūʿ and sujūd).
- Whose ṣalāh breaks? #strong[The man's], not the woman's --- because it
  is the man's duty to be ahead of the women, so the deficiency is
  attributed to him.

=== In ṭawāf
<in-awaf>
#strong[Muḥādhāt does NOT invalidate ṭawāf.]

#strong[Reason:] The ruling of muḥādhāt breaking ṣalāh is based on a
ḥadīth --- it is #strong[against qiyās] (analogy) and therefore
#strong[restricted to its specific context] (ṣalāh). It cannot be
extended to ṭawāf by analogy, because:

- Rulings that go against qiyās are #strong[restricted to their place].
- In ṭawāf, there is #strong[no ishtirāk (اشتراك)] \[joining/combining\]
  --- every person performs their own ṭawāf individually; no one leads
  another in ṭawāf.

#horizontalrule

== Part 5 --- Muwālāt (continuity between rounds)
<part-5-muwalat-continuity-between-rounds>
=== Ruling: NOT required
<ruling-not-required>
#strong[Muwālāt (موالاة)] --- performing all seven rounds of ṭawāf
#strong[consecutively] without any break --- is #strong[not] a condition
or wājib.

- A person #strong[may take breaks] during ṭawāf and #strong[resume from
  where he left off].
- There is #strong[no need to start over] from the beginning.

=== Dalīl
<dalil>
#quote(block: true)[
رُوِيَ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ ﷺ اسْتَسْقَى فِي الطَّوَافِ فَأُتِيَ بِمَاءٍ فَشَرِبَ

#emph["It is reported that the Prophet ﷺ asked for water during ṭawāf,
and water was brought to him, and he drank."]

#strong[Ref:] Hadith --- narrated regarding the Prophet ﷺ at the
#strong[Siqāyah] (the water station) (as cited in class --- confirm in
hadith index).
]

- The Prophet ﷺ #strong[took a break] to drink water during ṭawāf,
  demonstrating that muwālāt is #strong[not] required.
- This confirms that minor or even significant breaks do not invalidate
  the ṭawāf; the pilgrim simply continues from where he stopped.

