    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Khabar Mutawātir (خبر متواتر)]], [Narrated by a
    #strong[large number] of narrators in #strong[every era], starting
    from the #strong[era of the Ṣaḥābah]], [Ṣaḥābah era (1st
    generation)], [Can prove #strong[farḍiyyah (فرضية)]],
    [#strong[Khabar Mashhūr (خبر مشهور)]], [Narrated by a #strong[large
    number] but the fame reached that level in the #strong[era of the
    Tābiʿīn] (2nd generation)], [Tābiʿīn era (2nd generation)], [Can
    prove #strong[farḍiyyah]],
    [#strong[Khabar Wāḥid (خبر واحد)]], [Narrated by #strong[one or two]
    individuals in the first two eras; gained fame #strong[after] the
    eras of Ṣaḥābah and Tābiʿīn], [After 2nd generation], [Can prove
    #strong[wujūb] only --- #strong[not farḍiyyah]],
  )]
  , kind: table
  )

=== Why this matters
<why-this-matters>
- #strong[Ṣaḥābah] are #strong[all reliable] in matters of narration ---
  a ḥadīth with mass transmission from them leaves #strong[no room for
  doubt].
- #strong[Tābiʿīn] are the #strong[people of khayr (خير)] as the Prophet
  ﷺ himself testified --- mass narration from them also provides strong
  certainty.
- After these two eras, #strong[most ḥadīths] gained their fame --- they
  are ṣaḥīḥ if narrators are reliable, but carry a #strong[degree of
  doubt] in the transmission chain that prevents them from establishing
  #strong[farḍ].

=== Practical impact
<practical-impact>
#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (17.02%, 65.96%, 17.02%),
    align: (auto,auto,auto,),
    table.header([School], [Khabar Wāḥid with a command], [Result],),
    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Shāfiʿī]], [Can prove #strong[farḍ]], [No separate concept
    of wājib needed],
    [#strong[Ḥanafī]], [Can prove #strong[wujūb] only], [#strong[Farḍ]
    requires Qur'an / Mutawātir / Mashhūr evidence],
  )]
  , kind: table
  )

This is the #strong[root cause] of the recurring Ḥanafī-Shāfiʿī
differences on ṭahārah, satr al-ʿawrah, direction of ṭawāf, and other
conditions --- wherever the evidence is a #strong[khabar wāḥid], the
Ḥanafī school classifies the ruling as #strong[wājib] while the Shāfiʿī
school classifies it as #strong[farḍ].

#strong[The Shāfiʿī school has no concept of wājib] (as a category
between farḍ and sunnah) because they do not differentiate between the
three types of khabar in terms of what they can prove.

#strong[Practical difference between farḍ and wājib:]

- Both must be #strong[practised] --- no difference in obligation to
  act.
- The difference appears when the requirement is #strong[missed]:
  - Missing #strong[farḍ] → the action is #strong[completely invalid].
  - Missing #strong[wājib] → the action is #strong[valid but defective]
    --- compensation is possible.

#horizontalrule

== Part 8 --- Rulings of Nafl Tawaf
<part-8-rulings-of-nafl-tawaf>
All the above conditions and wājibāt apply to #strong[nafl ṭawāf] as
well --- once a nafl ṭawāf is #strong[started], it becomes #strong[wājib
to complete] it properly.

#strong[Key difference in penalty:] Because nafl ṭawāf is not wājib
#strong[by default] (it becomes wājib only after commencement), the
penalty for missing a wājib within it is #strong[lesser]:

