== Q&A
<qa>
#strong[Q:] People sometimes miss Tawaf al-Ziyarah because their flights
are early and they didn't get a chance. What is the ruling?

#strong[A:] Tawaf al-Ziyarah is a #strong[rukn (farḍ)] of Hajj. The
detailed ruling of what happens when it is missed --- and the
#strong[time period] within which it must be performed --- will be
discussed in a coming lesson. However, the teacher noted:

- #strong[Tawaf al-Ziyarah] is a part of #strong[Hajj itself] --- it is
  the #strong[second farḍ] (after Wuqūf ʿArafah).
- #strong[Tawaf al-Ṣadr] is #strong[not a part of Hajj] --- it is a
  separate wājib for outsiders when departing.
- The rulings for #strong[missing each] are different and will be
  addressed in the next class inshā'Allāh.

